BT
/F2 16 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 268 Tm
(21. Summary: All Layers Working Together) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 240 Tm
(Here is a complete trace of what happens when a cgroup agent tries to access a denied) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 225 Tm
(file through a symlink:) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 200 Tm
(Agent: ln -s /etc/shadow /tmp/trick && cat /tmp/trick) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 176 Tm
(Step 1: LANDLOCK CHECK \(inode level\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 164 Tm
(  Kernel resolves /tmp/trick ? symlink ? /etc/shadow ? inode #12345) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 152 Tm
(  Landlock: is inode #12345 in the allow set?) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 140 Tm
(    - inode\(/tmp\) is allowed, but /etc/shadow's inode is NOT under /tmp) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 128 Tm
(    - /etc/shadow's inode is under /etc, which is NOT in the allow set) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 116 Tm
(  Result: -EACCES ? BLOCKED AT FIRST LAYER) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 92 Tm
(  \(If Landlock were somehow bypassed, the next layers would catch it:\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 488 44 Tm
(Page 38 of 40) Tj
ET
endstream
