42 0 obj
<< /Length 3872 >>
stream
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 720 Tm
(Step 2: eBPF TRACEPOINT \(sys_enter_openat\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 708 Tm
(  Reads raw path: "/tmp/trick") Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 696 Tm
(  Is process in WATCHED_CGROUPS? YES \(cgroup ID match\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 684 Tm
(  Normalize path: "/tmp/trick" \(no proc/.. to strip\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 672 Tm
(  Evaluate policy: /tmp/** is allowed) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 660 Tm
(  ? Does NOT set PENDING_DENY \(raw path looks allowed\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 648 Tm
(  ? Sends event to userspace for logging) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 624 Tm
(Step 3: eBPF LSM \(file_open\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 612 Tm
(  Checks PENDING_DENY: not set ? allows) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 600 Tm
(  \(Landlock already blocked it, so this hook never fires\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 576 Tm
(Step 4: USERSPACE PROCESSING) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 564 Tm
(  Daemon receives event: agent tried to access /tmp/trick) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 552 Tm
(  Dashboard shows the access attempt in real-time events) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 540 Tm
(  Alert sent if configured) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 516 Tm
(Step 5: SECCOMP \(not triggered for normal file open\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 504 Tm
(  Would block io_uring if agent tried that instead) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 480 Tm
(Final result: Agent gets "Permission denied" from Landlock) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 468 Tm
(              Human operator sees the attempt in the dashboard) Tj
ET
BT
/F3 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 456 Tm
(              Audit trail records the event in SQLite) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 436 Tm
(This is defense-in-depth in action: Landlock stopped the attack at the first layer, but) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 421 Tm
(even if it had failed, the eBPF LSM and seccomp layers would have provided additional) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 406 Tm
(protection. And regardless of whether the access was blocked or allowed, the audit trail) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 391 Tm
(captures everything for forensic analysis.) Tj
ET
